a principal mountain, one of
 a class of seven mountains which are supposed to exist in each division
 of the continent; their names are:-- {#mahendro malayaH sahyaH SuktimAn#}
 {#fkzaparvataH . vinDyaSca pAriyAtraSca saptEte kulaparvatAH ..#}

.²1 well-born, of high birth; {#pradAne hi muniSrezWa kulaM niravaSezataH .#}
 {#vaktavyaM kulajAtena tanniboDa mahAmate ..#} <ls>Rām. 1. 71. 2</ls>.
.²2 ancestral, hereditary; <ls>Ki. 1. 31</ls> (used in both senses).

.²1 the head or chief of a family.
.²2 a sage who feeds and teaches 10,000 pupils; thus defined:-- {#munInAM#}
 {#daSasAhasraM yo'nnadAnAdipozaRAt . aDyApayati viprarzirasO kulapatiH smftaH#}
 {#.. api nAma kulapateriyamasavarRakzetrasaMBavA syAt#} <ls>Ś. 1</ls>; <ls>R. 1. 95</ls>; <ls>U. 3. 48</ls>.
.²3 The head-servant (<ls>Gīrvāṇa.</ls>); <ls>Bhāg. 5. 18. 1</ls>.
.²4 <ab>N.</ab> of Kṛṣṇa; {#kundasrajaH kulapateriha vAti ganDaH#} <ls>Bhāg. 10. 30. 11</ls>.

.²1 a respectable or high-born man; {#kaScumbati kulapuruzo veSyADarapallavaM#}
 {#maMnojYamapi#} <ls>Bh. 1. 59</ls>.
.²2 an ancestor.

